	'employers_s2_h' => 'The trial week and the monthly logbook',
	'employers_s2_p' => 'The trial week allows contractors and trainees to evaluate mutual compatibility on live jobs before making a long-term commitment. On day 3 of the trial week, Paloma Iturbe visits the job site to watch the candidate work alongside your team and discuss expectations. Once an apprenticeship agreement is signed, the student works four days a week with your firm and spends one day at the college workshop advancing practical skills. Throughout the three-year contract, employers maintain a monthly logbook documenting the trainee\'s work variety and hours. The employer\'s designated supervisor countersigns this logbook every month, ensuring systematic progression across domestic, commercial, and industrial installation work.',
