	'fees_intro' => 'We maintain a transparent, fixed fee structure with clear intake dates and strictly capped cohort sizes for every stage of training.',
	'fees_s1_h' => 'The six fixed fees',
	'fees_s1_p' => 'Our schedule of fees is fixed and identical across all college publications. The monthly Open board Saturday is completely free of charge, allowing prospective applicants to spend three hours trying a real cable termination with an instructor. The full-time twelve-week Foundation term costs €2,400. During week one, trainees purchase their permanent professional tool kit and personal protective equipment for €620. Once an apprentice is signed with an employer, the Apprenticeship tuition is €4,800 per year, paid directly by the employer over the three-year contract. For advanced students and qualified electricians, our ten-evening Inspection and testing module costs €1,150. If an apprentice fails an assessment piece, an individual practical re-assessment costs €180.',
