	'instructors_intro' => 'Our four permanent staff members bring decades of practical contracting, inspection, and site assessment experience directly to our workshop bays and partner sites.',
	'instructors_s1_h' => 'Ines Varga — Founder and Principal',
	'instructors_s1_p' => 'Ines Varga founded Akiha College in 1998 in a converted foundry shed after spending two decades working as an industrial installation electrician across Calder Quay. As principal, Ines directs college standards and personally leads our monthly open board Saturdays. She believes that hand skills, patience, and professional discipline form the bedrock of electrical safety. When watching an apprentice at the training board, Ines observes how they handle their tools, how carefully they organize their conductors, and whether they treat an unpowered board with the same rigorous isolation discipline demanded on a live industrial site.',
	'instructors_s2_h' => 'Rhea Lindqvist — Lead Instructor, Installation',
	'instructors_s2_p' => 'Rhea Lindqvist has served as our lead installation instructor since joining the college, supervising practical exercises across all four workshop bays. Rhea brings extensive experience from commercial infrastructure and architectural fit-out projects. In the workshop, she watches the precision of cable containment, the alignment of steel cable tray runs, and the neat dressing of conductors into multi-way distribution enclosures. Rhea demands that every wire stripped shows zero nicking of copper strands and that all terminal connections are torqued strictly to manufacturer specifications before she signs off an apprentice\'s work.',
	'instructors_s3_h' => 'Kofi Mensah — Instructor, Inspection and Testing',
	'instructors_s3_p' => 'Kofi Mensah directs our inspection, testing, and fault-finding curriculum, bringing deep expertise from industrial power distribution and motor control environments. Kofi oversees the Year 3 modules and evening specialist testing courses. In the testing bay, Kofi watches how trainees manipulate test leads, verify instrument calibration, and interpret resistance readings. He insists that apprentices understand the physics behind every measurement, requiring them to write out all testing sheets and calculations by hand before checking their conclusions against multifunction digital meters. No test certificate leaves Kofi\'s desk with an unverified figure.',
	'instructors_s4_h' => 'Paloma Iturbe — Site Assessor and Employer Liaison',
	'instructors_s4_p' => 'Paloma Iturbe coordinates our network of forty-one partner employers and conducts all formal site assessments across Calder Quay. Having managed large-scale building services and subcontracting teams, Paloma bridges the gap between college instruction and commercial site production. During her three annual full-day visits to each apprentice, Paloma watches how trainees manage active job-site hazards, coordinate with site managers, and integrate with experienced tradespeople. She ensures that partner employers provide genuine technical breadth and that trainees maintain rigorous professional standards away from the college.',
