	'news_privacy' => 'One letter a month. Unsubscribe any time; we never share your address.',
	'news_t' => 'Letters from the workshop',
	'newsletter_intro' => 'Receive monthly dispatches from our Calder Quay workshop covering intake deadlines, open board schedules, and practical installation notes.',
	'newsletter_s1_h' => 'Letters from the workshop floor',
	'newsletter_s1_p' => 'Our monthly newsletter is written directly from the workshop bays at Foundry Row 9. Each dispatch provides practical, grounded insight into electrical craft and vocational training. We share updates on upcoming intake deadlines for our January and September cohorts, announce open board Saturday dates, and report on the technical work our apprentices are completing across Calder Quay. In addition, each edition includes a dedicated technical note written by instructors Rhea Lindqvist or Kofi Mensah, discussing common installation challenges such as proper glanding technique, safe isolation verification, or accurate handwritten test documentation. There are no advertising banners, sponsored marketing content, or promotional fluff.',
	'newsletter_s2_h' => 'Dispatch frequency and subscriber privacy',
	'newsletter_s2_p' => 'We respect your inbox and believe communication should remain measured and purposeful. We send exactly one letter per month, dispatched on the first Tuesday following our monthly open board Saturday. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link included at the bottom of every email. We maintain strict confidentiality with subscriber data: your email address will never be sold, rented, or shared with third parties or advertising brokers. It is used exclusively to deliver our workshop updates directly from Akiha College admissions.',
