	'older' => 'Older',
	'open_board_intro' => 'Held on the first Saturday of every month, our free open board sessions give prospective trainees three hours of hands-on cable termination experience with an instructor.',
	'open_board_s1_h' => 'First Saturday of each month',
	'open_board_s1_p' => 'On the first Saturday of each month, Akiha College opens its workshop doors from 09:00 to 12:00 for our free Open board session. Led personally by college founder Ines Varga alongside our instructional staff, these three-hour mornings are designed for school leavers, career changers, and parents who want to inspect our training facilities. There are no sales presentations, slides, or promotional lectures. Visitors step directly into bay two, put on clear safety glasses, and stand in front of our plywood training boards to experience how professional electrical installation training is conducted in Calder Quay.',
	'open_board_s2_h' => 'Trying a termination at the board',
	'open_board_s2_p' => 'During your three hours at the board, an instructor guides you through terminating an armoured cable into a metal isolator enclosure. You will measure and strip the tough outer PVC sheath, cut and flare steel wire armouring, and secure a brass mechanical cable gland using proper spanners. Next, you will strip the inner insulation cleanly without scoring copper conductors, route the cores into terminal blocks, and torque each screw to specification. This hands-on exercise lets you experience the physical patience, mechanical dexterity, and spatial awareness required in our daily trade before you submit a formal application.',
	'open_board_s3_h' => 'Workshop clothing and practical preparation',
	'open_board_s3_p' => 'To attend an Open board Saturday, you do not need prior electrical experience or personal tools. We supply all cables, glands, hand tools, and safety eyewear. You must arrive wearing durable, practical clothing such as denim or heavy cotton work trousers, and sturdy flat footwear or work boots; open-toed shoes and soft trainers are strictly prohibited in the workshop. The session starts promptly at 09:00, so please arrive ten minutes early at Foundry Row 9, Calder Quay. Tea and coffee are provided midway through the morning while instructors answer questions about upcoming intakes and employer sponsorships.',
	'open_board_s4_h' => 'Reserving your place at the board',
	'open_board_s4_p' => 'Because workshop bay capacity is strictly limited to twenty-four workstations, prospective visitors must reserve a place in advance. To secure your bench, complete our online booking form or send an email directly to hello@akiha-college.example with the subject line \'Open board booking — Akiha College\'. Please include your full name, contact phone number, and preferred date. If you need assistance or wish to confirm availability for an upcoming first Saturday, contact our admissions office at +00 20 7410 0388 between 09:00 and 17:00, Monday through Friday.',
